 the 5-field _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST, so parent/reporter-only branch-3 payloads are not misclassified as inert; also correct 'no batch_dispatch import' to name the true allowlist home (dispatch_apply_phases.py).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["dispatch_apply_phases.py:73: _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({\"summary\", \"description\", \"assignee\", \"priority\", \"status\"}) — matches the plan's list","dispatch_one.py:499: `_has_parent_op = _update_one_apply_parent(fields, ...)` pops `parent` before the allowlist filter and routes via client.set_parent (dispatch_one.py:538-560)","dispatch_apply_phases.py:273-287: reporter is popped and routed via client.set_reporter","outbound_fields.py:399 + dispatch_one.py:547 both note these fields are deliberately NOT in _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST yet still reach Jira","binding_walk.py:265 shows changed_fields can legitimately carry non-allowlist keys"],"finding":"The plan's inline 'Jira-reachable' survival set is limited to the _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST 5 fields (summary, description, assignee, priority, status), but `parent` and `reporter` are also Jira-reachable outbound sinks — they are popped from the payload and routed via client.set_parent / client.set_reporter BEFORE the allowlist filter, and are intentionally NOT in _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST. A branch-3 changed_fields payload whose only genuine change is `parent` or `reporter` would be misclassified as inert and skipped, dropping real outbound work.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc4d73d462754be3e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status)'","norm_id":"n469d0bfe0eb5f4e2","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket is reparented locally (or its epic-link cleared) with no other field change; branch-3 builds changed_fields={'parent': ...}; the plan's survival test finds no allowlisted field differing and skips the emit — the parent op never reaches client.set_parent (this is the exact ~230-mutation parent regression class referenced in dispatch_one.py:547-552).","A reporter-only change is similarly skipped."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the survival set as _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST plus {'parent', 'reporter'} — i.e. every field the outbound update path can actually push, including those popped-and-routed before the allowlist filter. Add a negative-control AC covering a parent-only (and reporter-only) branch-3 change that MUST still emit.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Broaden the plan's 'Jira-reachable' field set to include `parent` and `reporter` (routed via set_parent/set_reporter before the allowlist filter), not just `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST`, so a branch-3 update whose sole surviving delta is parent/reporter is NOT skipped as inert.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["dispatch_apply_phases.py:73 `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({\"summary\", \"description\", \"assignee\", \"priority\", \"status\"})` — matches the plan's list, but is applied only to the SCALAR edit","dispatch_one.py:499-501: `_update_one_apply_parent(...)` and `_update_one_apply_reporter(...)` run BEFORE `_update_one_filter_fields`, popping `parent`/`reporter` and routing them via set_parent/set_reporter","dispatch_apply_phases.py:260-266: reporter 'Pops reporter off fields BEFORE the allowlist filter (so it never reaches the scalar edit and need not be allowlisted)'; dispatch_one.py:547 confirms parent was intentionally NOT added to the allowlist because it routes via set_parent","config.py:8 `EXCLUDED_FIELDS = (\"local_id\", \"rebar-id\")` — parent/reporter are NOT excluded, so differ.py:579-597 can place them in `changed`"],"finding":"The plan's inert definition restricts Jira-reachable fields to `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` (summary, description, assignee, priority, status), but the outbound update path also reaches Jira for `parent` (via client.set_parent) and `reporter` (via client.set_reporter), which are popped from the fields dict BEFORE the allowlist filter in dispatch_apply_phases. Neither is in EXCLUDED_FIELDS (only local_id, rebar-id), so branch-3's resolved `changed` dict can legitimately contain only `parent` or `reporter`. The plan's survival test would classify such a mutation as inert and skip its emit, silently dropping a real Jira write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f192f4ce3950eafd6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status)'","norm_id":"ne30b9d95cbc19cd5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A key-set-prev pass where the only resolved delta on a both-sides key is `parent` (reparent/detach) or `reporter`","A branch-3 mutation whose scalar allowlisted fields all match Jira but whose parent/reporter differs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the survival set as the allowlisted scalars PLUS the fields dispatched by dedicated sub-calls before the allowlist filter (`parent`, `reporter`); keep a mutation whenever any of those resolved values differs from `jira_fields.get(field)`. Cite dispatch_apply_phases.py (allowlist + reporter pop) and dispatch_one.py:499 (parent pop) as the source of the reachable-field set.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Avoid hardcoding a parallel five-field allowlist in differ.py: reference/extract the existing `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` (dispatch_apply_phases.py:73) into a shared pure leaf, OR add a test that pins differ.py's inline set equal to `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` so the two cannot drift.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0611,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["dispatch_apply_phases.py:73: `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({\"summary\", \"description\", \"assignee\", \"priority\", \"status\"})` — the exact same five fields the plan enumerates","dispatch_apply_phases.py:64-73 comment: the typed leaf and batch path were deliberately made to 'apply the same allowlist' — this constant IS the 'stripped before update_issue' filter the plan's inertness definition relies on","apply_outbound.py:184 comment records prior drift of exactly this shape: 'the two drifted: bug 3f04 dropped outbound links because the capability was re-added to the batch path while the differ/tests exercised only this leaf'","Grep confirms the allowlist has no shared/config home (only dispatch_apply_phases.py defines it); an inline copy in differ.py would be the second definition"],"finding":"The plan hardcodes the Jira-reachable field set {summary, description, assignee, priority, status} inline in differ.py, duplicating the canonical `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` frozenset that already exists as the single stripping allowlist, creating a second source of truth that can silently drift.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffb24cb1725517cff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Approach' section: 'retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status)'; Files: differ.py","norm_id":"n8a5f8a7db064037a","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future story adds a sixth pushable field (e.g. re-enables 'issuetype' or adds 'labels-as-scalar') to `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` but not to differ.py's inline copy: the differ then wrongly classifies a real mutation as inert and skips it, silently losing an outbound update — the failure mode AC2's negative control is meant to catch but only for today's field set.","The reverse drift: a field removed from the batch allowlist but left in differ.py resurrects the ~516-inert-mutation regression this ticket exists to fix."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extract the five-field allowlist to a small pure/constant-only module (e.g. alongside mutation_payloads or a new field-contract leaf) that both differ.py and dispatch_apply_phases.py import, so there is one source of truth without differ.py taking a runtime dependency on the heavy dispatch_apply_phases module. If extraction is out of scope, add a unit test asserting differ.py's inline set == dispatch_apply_phases._OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either source the accepted-Jira-field set from a shared constant (not a re-typed inline literal) or add a test/assertion pinning differ.py's inline list to the fields the Jira update path actually accepts, so the two cannot drift.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan hardcodes the field list inline in differ.py while explicitly avoiding a batch_dispatch import","The field list is the authoritative contract shared with the Jira update path; duplicating it introduces drift risk"],"finding":"The accepted-field set (summary, description, assignee, priority, status) is duplicated inline in differ.py rather than derived from the single source used by the Jira update path, so if update_issue's accepted fields change the two lists silently drift and could wrongly suppress a genuine mutation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff2ca1817cfccf190","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'compute the survival test inline in differ.py (no batch_dispatch import) ... retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status)'","norm_id":"n20d1f5cc3f31b770","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later ticket adds a new field to the Jira update path (e.g. labels); differ.py's stale inline list omits it and re-suppresses a now-genuine mutation"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reference a shared module-level constant for the Jira-reachable field set consumed by both the differ survival test and the update path, or add a unit test asserting equality of differ.py's inline set against the update path's accepted set.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","diverg